# Wizden Project Rules

This is a Space Station 14 content fork (Wizden). Follow upstream SS14/Robust Toolbox ECS architecture and the Wizden-specific placement rules below.

**Do not edit `RobustToolbox/`.** It is a separate engine project (read-only submodule). All work belongs in Wizden content; see `robust-toolbox-readonly.mdc`.

## Wizden File Placement

### New original content — put it in Wizden folders

All **new** Wizden code and assets belong under Wizden folder structures, mirroring existing layout:

| Area | Location |
|------|----------|
| Server systems | `Content.Server/Wizden/` or `Content.Server/_Wizden/` |
| Shared components, events, systems | `Content.Shared/Wizden/` or `Content.Shared/_Wizden/` |
| Client systems, UI | `Content.Client/Wizden/` or `Content.Client/_Wizden/` |
| YAML prototypes | `Resources/Prototypes/_Wizden/` |
| Maps | `Resources/Maps/**/Wizden/` |
| Textures / audio | `Resources/Textures/**/Wizden/`, `Resources/Audio/**/Wizden/` as appropriate |

Organize by feature (e.g. `Content.Server/Wizden/Example/ExampleSystem.cs`, `Content.Shared/Wizden/Example/ExampleComponent.cs`). Use file-scoped namespaces matching the folder path (e.g. `namespace Content.Server.Wizden.Example;`).

Do **not** add new standalone features as loose files outside Wizden paths.

### Editing upstream files — mark every change with `//Wizden`

When modifying **existing** files that are **not** inside a Wizden subfolder, annotate every changed line or block:

**Single-line change** — append `//Wizden` (optional short note):

```csharp
using Content.Server.Wizden.Chat; //Wizden
public int Range { get; private set; } = 6; //Wizden: 10>6 to reduce spam
```

**Multi-line block** — wrap with begin/end comments:

```csharp
//Wizden - Begin
public void SetYield(SeedData seed, int newYield)
{
    seed.Yield = newYield;
}
//Wizden - End
```

Also acceptable: `//Wizden Block start` / `//Wizden block end`, or descriptive variants like `//Wizden - FeatureName Start`.

Apply the same rule to YAML edits in non-Wizden prototype files when adding or changing Wizden content inline.

Files already under `Wizden/` or `_Wizden/` paths do **not** need these markers.

