## SS14 Coding Conventions

Reference: [SS14 Conventions wiki](https://docs.spacestation14.com/en/general-development/codebase-info/conventions.html)

### General

- No copy-paste — extract shared helpers. No magic strings/numbers — use `const`, `static readonly`, or `ProtoId<T>`.
- Comment **why**, not what. Use XML docs on public APIs and `[DataField]` members.
- Human-readable text via localization (`Loc.GetString`), never as dictionary keys or identifiers.
- Fields and auto-properties before methods. File-scoped namespaces. One parameter per line when signatures wrap.

### Prototypes & resources

- Prefer **prototypes over enums** for in-game types.
- Don't cache prototypes — store `ProtoId<T>` and resolve via `IPrototypeManager`.
- Sounds: `SoundSpecifier` / `SoundCollectionSpecifier`. Sprites: `SpriteSpecifier`.
- Use CVars or constants for tunable values.

### Performance & style

- Prefer event-driven logic over per-tick `Update()` when possible.
- Classes must be `sealed`, `abstract`, `static`, or `[Virtual]`.
- No extension methods on `EntityUid`, components, or entity systems — use system public methods.
- UI: prefer XAML over pure C# UI definitions.
- Avoid variable captures in lambdas passed to hot paths; use overloads that accept custom state.

### Entity system example (pattern to follow)

```csharp
public sealed class FooSystem : EntitySystem
{
    [Dependency] private readonly SharedAppearanceSystem _appearance = default!;

    public override void Initialize()
    {
        SubscribeLocalEvent<FooComponent, ComponentInit>(OnFooInit);
        SubscribeLocalEvent<FooComponent, InteractUsingEvent>(OnInteract);
    }

    public void SetCounter(Entity<FooComponent?> ent, int count)
    {
        if (!Resolve(ent, ref ent.Comp))
            return;

        ent.Comp.InteractCounter = count;
        RaiseLocalEvent(ent, new FooCounterChangedEvent(count));
    }
}
```
